<i>Jesus vs. Satan</i>

249
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,252
<i>Live from the
South Park Forum on Saturday!</i>

250
00:09:45,377 --> 00:09:48,463
<i>Call now to order.
Only $49.95.</i>

251
00:09:48,589 --> 00:09:50,966
Hey, wait a minute.
Saturday is my birthday party!

252
00:09:51,091 --> 00:09:52,509
They can't have
the fight on Saturday!

253
00:09:52,634 --> 00:09:53,969
I don't know

254
00:09:54,094 --> 00:09:55,679
what to do, dude.
Do we go to the fight

255
00:09:55,804 --> 00:09:57,931
or Cartman's birthday?
- Cartman's birthday.

256
00:09:58,056 --> 00:09:59,558
We can't miss the final
apocalyptic battle

257
00:09:59,683 --> 00:10:01,393
between good and evil.
- You guys,

258
00:10:01,518 --> 00:10:03,145
my mom's getting
a Ferris wheel.

259
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:05,939
Well, c'mon we have to
at least see the weigh-in.

260
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:07,316
Who the hell decided
the fight

261
00:10:07,441 --> 00:10:09,109
had to be on Saturday, huh?

262
00:10:09,234 --> 00:10:10,777
This whole thing is a plot
against me, isn't it?

263
00:10:14,489 --> 00:10:16,533
When is Satan gonna show up?

264
00:10:16,658 --> 00:10:18,493
Did the devil show up yet?
- Not yet.

265
00:10:18,619 --> 00:10:20,412
Hey Jesus,
if you win the fight

266
00:10:20,537 --> 00:10:22,998
can you turn Kenny
back to normal?

267
00:10:23,123 --> 00:10:24,958
What the hell do you mean
"if" I win the fight?

268
00:10:25,083 --> 00:10:26,960
Don't mind him, Jesus.
He's Jewish.

269
00:10:27,085 --> 00:10:28,795
Oh.
- We're all with you Jesus.

270
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,798
We put every dime we have on
you beating that Dark Prince.

271
00:10:31,923 --> 00:10:34,051
Thank you for your faith,

272
00:10:34,176 --> 00:10:35,844
but I think perhaps
you don't understand

273
00:10:35,969 --> 00:10:37,346
the severity of the situation.

274
00:10:37,471 --> 00:10:39,848
You're gonna kick his ass,
Jesus.

275
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:46,480
Behold,
the evil one approaches.

276
00:10:49,316 --> 00:10:52,527
Holy poop-on-a-stick!

277
00:10:52,653 --> 00:10:54,905
Puny son of Jehovah.

278
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:58,992
Prepare to enter
thy house of pain.

279
00:11:00,243 --> 00:11:03,038
Holy crap, dude.
Satan is huge!

280
00:11:03,163 --> 00:11:05,999
Now that is a man
who has eaten a lot of beef.

281
00:11:06,124 --> 00:11:07,751
Son of God,

282
00:11:07,876 --> 00:11:11,338
I will smash thy face
into small little bits.

283
00:11:11,463 --> 00:11:13,507
Oh...oh, yeah?
- Damn.

284
00:11:13,632 --> 00:11:15,884
I have
such delightful horrors

285
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:18,595
to unleash upon thee.

286
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,097
Oh, yeah?

287
00:11:22,474 --> 00:11:24,476
Satan weighs in at...

288
00:11:24,601 --> 00:11:27,896
320 pounds, 4 ounces.

289
00:11:30,774 --> 00:11:33,485
Jesus Christ weighs in at...

290
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:36,113
135 pounds, 1 ounce.

291
00:11:36,238 --> 00:11:38,448
Oh, crap.

292
00:11:38,573 --> 00:11:40,283
Ah, c'mon,
I weigh more than that!

293
00:11:40,409 --> 00:11:43,870
Let the new prince
be decided on Saturday.

294
00:11:43,995 --> 00:11:47,457
First South Park,
then the world.

295
00:11:49,710 --> 00:11:52,379
Well, I think I'll...

296
00:11:52,504 --> 00:11:54,089
I think I left the oven on.

297
00:11:54,214 --> 00:11:57,968
Yeah, I think
I left your oven on, too.

298
00:11:59,386 --> 00:12:02,723
See you Saturday, Jesus.
Good luck.

299
00:12:04,516 --> 00:12:06,643
Change my bet!
- Put my money on the devil!

300
00:12:06,768 --> 00:12:08,437
I want to change my bet
to Satan.

301
00:12:08,562 --> 00:12:10,856
Me too.
- Hey, wait. I was here first.

302
00:12:10,981 --> 00:12:13,442
Now, as your counselor,

303
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:17,279
I want you to feel like you can
tell me anything, m'kay?

304
00:12:17,404 --> 00:12:19,197
Being the new kid can be tough,

305
00:12:19,322 --> 00:12:22,617
but I'm your friend, m'kay?
- Everybody hates me.

306
00:12:22,743 --> 00:12:26,079
Well why do you suppose
that is?

307
00:12:26,204 --> 00:12:27,622
Because I'm the son
of the devil?

308
00:12:27,748 --> 00:12:30,292
Uh-huh, that's a good start.
Why else?

309
00:12:30,417 --> 00:12:32,544
Because I burn them
and kill them?

310
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:34,463
Well, yeah, maybe that's it.

311
00:12:34,588 --> 00:12:36,923
What you need to do, Damien

312
00:12:37,048 --> 00:12:39,009
is to be overly nice.

313
00:12:39,134 --> 00:12:42,137
No matter how mean
the other kids are to you,

314
00:12:42,262 --> 00:12:43,889
just don't retaliate.

315
00:12:44,014 --> 00:12:45,682
Be passive, m'kay.

316
00:12:45,807 --> 00:12:47,684
That's what I taught
the little British boy, Pip,

317
00:12:47,809 --> 00:12:51,104
and just look at how much the
other children like him now.

318
00:12:51,229 --> 00:12:53,607
I bet I can
spit the most on him.

319
00:12:53,732 --> 00:12:56,651
Oh yeah, I bet I can
spit in his hair.

320
00:12:56,777 --> 00:12:59,362
Nice try, a little higher
and you've got it.

321
00:12:59,488 --> 00:13:02,115
Man, recess sucks
without any slides or nothing.

322
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:04,409
Oh, here comes the
unholy butthole now.

323
00:13:04,534 --> 00:13:06,077
Hey, thanks a lot

324
00:13:06,203 --> 00:13:07,996
for burning everything down,
you little bitch.

325
00:13:08,121 --> 00:13:10,373
I apologize
for ruining your playground

326
00:13:10,499 --> 00:13:13,001
and turning your friend
into a duck-billed platypus.

327
00:13:13,126 --> 00:13:14,503
I was doing my
father's bidding.

328
00:13:14,628 --> 00:13:16,171
I didn't have a choice.

329
00:13:16,963 --> 00:13:19,633
Oh, excuse me, new kid

330
00:13:19,758 --> 00:13:22,928
I didn't mean to fart on you
I didn't have a choice.

331
00:13:23,053 --> 00:13:25,639
Hoo, you stink, new kid.
You smell like a fart.

332
00:13:25,764 --> 00:13:28,016
Yeah, we're gonna call you
Fartboy from now on.

333
00:13:28,141 --> 00:13:29,851
Bye-bye, Fartboy.
- See ya.

334
00:13:29,976 --> 00:13:31,645
Good day.
How are you, Damien?

335
00:13:31,770 --> 00:13:33,563
Those guys farted on me
and then called me--

336
00:13:33,688 --> 00:13:35,065
Fartboy?
Oh, good.

337
00:13:35,190 --> 00:13:36,775
Perhaps they won't
call me that anymore.

338
00:13:41,655 --> 00:13:44,324
Excuse me...

339
00:13:44,449 --> 00:13:46,535
I just talked to the bookie
at the sports betting bar.

340
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:48,662
Uh-oh.

341
00:13:48,787 --> 00:13:51,331
I have been forsaken!
It seems that several bets

342
00:13:51,456 --> 00:13:53,708
were changed to Satan
this morning.

343
00:13:53,834 --> 00:13:56,378
In fact it seems that
only one person

344
00:13:56,503 --> 00:13:58,797
in this entire town
is still betting on me.

345
00:13:58,922 --> 00:14:01,383
You should all be ashamed
of yourselves.

346
00:14:01,508 --> 00:14:03,301
Betting against
your lord and savior.

347
00:14:03,426 --> 00:14:04,928
I am disgusted!

348
00:14:05,053 --> 00:14:06,721
Your bet was
changed as well.

349
00:14:06,847 --> 00:14:08,139
You forsaked me too.

350
00:14:08,265 --> 00:14:10,392
Oh.
Right, well...

351
00:14:10,517 --> 00:14:12,561
he does have a couple hundred
pounds on you, Jesus.

352
00:14:12,686 --> 00:14:15,146
I implore you all,
don't bet on the Dark One.

353
00:14:15,272 --> 00:14:16,815
It is a bet that
you will never win.

354
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:19,442
Jesus, I am sorry
I have sinned against you.

355
00:14:19,568 --> 00:14:21,278
I'm gonna march right over
to that bookie

356
00:14:21,403 --> 00:14:22,737
and change my bet right now.

357
00:14:22,863 --> 00:14:24,823
Oh, yeah, yeah me too.
Me too.

358
00:14:24,948 --> 00:14:27,284
Yeah.
- Praise the Lord!

359
00:14:27,409 --> 00:14:30,871
Thank you sweet Jesus
for showing us the light!

360
00:14:30,996 --> 00:14:33,123
See you later.

361
00:14:34,583 --> 00:14:36,668
What the hell does he think,
we're all crazy?

362
00:14:36,793 --> 00:14:39,170
Yeah, crazy.

363
00:14:39,296 --> 00:14:41,756
This show's gay.
- Yeah.

364
00:14:41,882 --> 00:14:43,925
You're all
a bunch of Judases.

365
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,510
Hey Jesus.

366
00:14:45,635 --> 00:14:47,137
What are you doing
out so late, kids?

367
00:14:47,262 --> 00:14:48,680
We have to find
Red and Green Mega Mans

368
00:14:48,805 --> 00:14:50,432
for Cartman's birthday party.
- Oh.

369
00:14:50,557 --> 00:14:53,518
Kids, you believe
I can beat Satan, right?

370
00:14:53,643 --> 00:14:55,228
Sure, dude.
You're the son of god!

371
00:14:55,353 --> 00:14:57,188
Yeah. You aren't having
any doubts, are you?

372
00:14:57,314 --> 00:14:58,690
N-no, no.

373
00:14:58,815 --> 00:15:01,610
But could you help me train
a little?

374
00:15:02,611 --> 00:15:05,530
Satan, what do expect
the outcome of the fight to be?

375
00:15:05,655 --> 00:15:08,867
I will crush him
like a little bug.

376
00:15:08,992 --> 00:15:11,161
Satan, what about
the rumors of your involvement

377
00:15:11,286 --> 00:15:13,830
in the Gulf War?

378
00:15:13,955 --> 00:15:15,790
Let's focus on the fight,
can we please?

379
00:15:15,916 --> 00:15:18,501
I'm so sick of people talking
smack about my fighters.

380
00:15:18,627 --> 00:15:20,670
All this, "He's mean",
"He's a dirty fighter",

381
00:15:20,795 --> 00:15:22,339
"He's the cause
for all the violence and death

382
00:15:22,464 --> 00:15:24,174
in the world."
It's just getting old.

383
00:15:24,299 --> 00:15:27,469
Let's just let everything
be decided in the ring.

384
00:15:27,594 --> 00:15:29,346
You guys,
shouldn't you be out shopping

385
00:15:29,471 --> 00:15:31,181
for my birthday presents?
- Here, Jesus,

386
00:15:31,306 --> 00:15:33,433
drink these raw eggs.
- No way, dude.

387
00:15:33,558 --> 00:15:35,310
I-I can't.

388
00:15:35,435 --> 00:15:36,895
I can't hit Jesus Christ.

389
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:39,230
My mother would never
speak to me again.

390
00:15:39,356 --> 00:15:40,774
But you're his
sparing partner, Chef.

391
00:15:40,899 --> 00:15:42,067
Yeah, you have to hit him.

392
00:15:42,192 --> 00:15:43,818
Satan must be defeated, Chef.

393
00:15:43,944 --> 00:15:46,613
Please help me to train.
- Okay...

394
00:15:46,738 --> 00:15:48,949
But I'm just gonna tap you,
all right?

395
00:15:49,074 --> 00:15:50,408
Give it your best shot--oh!

396
00:15:50,533 --> 00:15:53,370
Oh, God in heaven.
What have I done?

397
00:15:53,495 --> 00:15:55,914
Anybody get the number
of that truck?

398
00:16:01,628 --> 00:16:04,506
C'mon kiddies, eat more.

399
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:07,092
Welcome, Clyde.
Please put your present

400
00:16:07,217 --> 00:16:08,718
on the table to your left.

401
00:16:08,843 --> 00:16:11,346
Welcome, Debbie.
Presents go to your left.

402
00:16:11,471 --> 00:16:12,597
Welcome, Chef.
- Yep.

403
00:16:12,722 --> 00:16:14,307
Here's your present, children.

404
00:16:14,432 --> 00:16:16,810
Well, nice party.
See you later.

405
00:16:16,935 --> 00:16:18,353
Hey, you just got here, Chef.

406
00:16:18,478 --> 00:16:20,563
I know,
but the fight is starting.

407
00:16:20,689 --> 00:16:23,316
But, dude, check it out.
Cartman's mom made chili.

408
00:16:23,441 --> 00:16:25,527
Mm.
- Mmm.

409
00:16:25,652 --> 00:16:27,862
That's my favorite
kind of chili.

410
00:16:27,988 --> 00:16:30,448
I guess all the kids are at
that fat boy's birthday party.

411
00:16:30,573 --> 00:16:32,283
Yes.
It's always such a huge event.

412
00:16:32,409 --> 00:16:33,910
Sometimes I like
to sneak up to the fence

413
00:16:34,035 --> 00:16:36,037
and close my eyes
and pretend I'm there.

414
00:16:36,162 --> 00:16:37,706
The other kids
have always hated you?

415
00:16:37,831 --> 00:16:39,666
Oh, yes.
Actually, I think they make fun

416
00:16:39,791 --> 00:16:41,793
of the fat boy a lot too.
But now I think they like him

417
00:16:41,918 --> 00:16:43,211
because he picks on me.

418
00:16:46,881 --> 00:16:49,009
In the blue corner,
wearing white trunks,

419
00:16:49,134 --> 00:16:52,554
weighing in
at a mere 140 pounds,

420
00:16:52,679 --> 00:16:53,847
Jesús

421
00:16:53,972 --> 00:16:55,932
"El Savior"

422
00:16:56,057 --> 00:16:57,934
Christ.

423
00:17:00,270 --> 00:17:02,772
And in the very, very,
black corner

424
00:17:02,897 --> 00:17:05,191
wearing very,
very black trunks.

425
00:17:05,316 --> 00:17:07,861
The king of all
that is evil...

426
00:17:07,986 --> 00:17:11,406
Beelzebub!

427
00:17:16,411 --> 00:17:18,288
Ladies and gentlemen,

428
00:17:18,413 --> 00:17:23,668
let's get ready to rumble!

429
00:17:23,793 --> 00:17:25,587
Okay, I want a good,
clean fight, guys.

430
00:17:25,712 --> 00:17:28,423
No punches below the belt,
holding, or miracles.

431
00:17:32,927 --> 00:17:35,013
Hey! What the hell
do you think you're doing here?

432
00:17:35,138 --> 00:17:37,015
Yeah you aren't invited,
new kid.

433
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:39,184
And neither are you, Pip.
- Yes, I tried to tell Damien

434
00:17:39,309 --> 00:17:40,685
that we weren't invited, but--
- Wait a minute.

435
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:42,270
Give me a chance!

436
00:17:42,395 --> 00:17:44,606
I want to do something special
for your party!

437
00:17:51,404 --> 00:17:52,655
Oh, no!

438
00:17:55,784 --> 00:17:57,619
Wow.
- Whoa, that was cool.

439
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:00,455
Hey, you're not
such a bad guy,

440
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:01,998
after all, Damien.
- Yeah.

441
00:18:02,123 --> 00:18:04,501
Come on in
and join the party.

442
00:18:06,753 --> 00:18:08,171
Oh!

443
00:18:10,548 --> 00:18:12,717
Oh!

444
00:18:15,929 --> 00:18:18,890
C'mon you little wuss,
fight!

445
00:18:19,015 --> 00:18:20,767
Throw a punch.

446
00:18:20,892 --> 00:18:24,479
Oh, I wonder what Stan got me
for my birthday present.

447
00:18:24,604 --> 00:18:28,233
Oh, look a Blue Mega Man!
Thank you, Stan.

448
00:18:28,358 --> 00:18:31,277
You may eat pie and cake
and ice cream now.

449
00:18:31,402 --> 00:18:32,862
And what did Wendy get me?

450
00:18:32,987 --> 00:18:35,657
Oh, it's the Yellow Mega Man!

451
00:18:35,782 --> 00:18:38,159
Help yourself to pie, cake,
and ice cream, Wendy.

452
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:40,036
Oh, look what Kyle got me.

453
00:18:40,161 --> 00:18:41,663
It's a Red Mega--

454
00:18:41,788 --> 00:18:43,748
Ants in the Pants?
Ants in the pan--

455
00:18:43,873 --> 00:18:45,166
Ants in the pants!

456
00:18:45,291 --> 00:18:46,584
It's game, dude.
It's really fun!

457
00:18:46,709 --> 00:18:48,878
You son of a bitch!
- Ah!

458
00:18:49,003 --> 00:18:51,005
You were supposed to get me
the Red Mega Man!

459
00:18:51,131 --> 00:18:53,049
Now I can't make
Ultra Mega Mega Man!

460
00:18:53,174 --> 00:18:54,968
You dirty, cheap-ass,
piece of crap.

461
00:18:55,093 --> 00:18:56,427
They were all out of 'em,
dude!

462
00:18:56,553 --> 00:18:58,930
I hate you!
I want you to die!

463
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,306
Die!

464
00:19:00,431 --> 00:19:02,225
That's it!
Party is over!

465
00:19:02,350 --> 00:19:04,060
Everybody go home!

466
00:19:08,481 --> 00:19:09,983
Get the hell out I said!

467
00:19:10,108 --> 00:19:12,694
Party's over!
Get out God damn it!

468
00:19:12,819 --> 00:19:14,279
Whoa, dude,
you need to mellow out.

469
00:19:14,404 --> 00:19:16,781
Take your stupid
Ants in the Pants with you!

470
00:19:16,906 --> 00:19:19,325
Wow, that kid has
some real emotional problems.

471
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:20,785
Ah, he does this
all the time.

472
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:22,620
C'mon children,
we can still catch

473
00:19:22,745 --> 00:19:25,123
the end of the fight.

474
00:19:26,583 --> 00:19:28,710
Oh, what a splendid party!

475
00:19:31,087 --> 00:19:32,672
Oh!

476
00:19:32,797 --> 00:19:34,465
Fight, damn it.

477
00:19:37,594 --> 00:19:39,846
Ow!

478
00:19:41,681 --> 00:19:43,558
Dude, Jesus is getting
his butt kicked.

479
00:19:43,683 --> 00:19:46,269
You've got to fight, Jesus.

480
00:19:46,394 --> 00:19:47,896
Why, what's the point?

481
00:19:48,021 --> 00:19:49,230
No one believes in me.

482
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:50,940
Everyone put their money
on Satan.

483
00:19:51,065 --> 00:19:53,401
My father forsaked me,
the town forsaked me.

484
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:55,195
I'm completely forsook.

485
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:57,113
Somebody bet on you, Jesus.
You said yourself

486
00:19:57,238 --> 00:19:58,907
that one person
still has money on you.

487
00:19:59,032 --> 00:20:00,533
It doesn't matter.
He's way too strong

488
00:20:00,658 --> 00:20:02,118
for me anyway
I give up.

489
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:03,912
God damn it, Jesus,
snap out of it!

490
00:20:04,037 --> 00:20:05,496
What would Nancy Kerrigan do,
huh?

491
00:20:05,622 --> 00:20:06,998
Nancy Kerrigan
wouldn't give up.

492
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:08,583
When things were
looking their darkest

493
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:10,168
Nancy Kerrigan fought
to be the best.

494
00:20:10,293 --> 00:20:12,086
She wouldn't stop
until she was number one.

495
00:20:12,212 --> 00:20:13,546
Uh, Stan.
- Nancy Kerrigan wouldn't

496
00:20:13,671 --> 00:20:15,340
settle for second best.
- Stan.

497
00:20:15,465 --> 00:20:16,633
She wouldn't quit until
she brought home the gold.

498
00:20:16,758 --> 00:20:18,134
Stan!
- What?

499
00:20:18,259 --> 00:20:19,677
Nancy Kerrigan got
the silver, dude.

500
00:20:19,802 --> 00:20:21,638
She came in second.

501
00:20:22,764 --> 00:20:24,307
Really?
- Yeah, dude.

502
00:20:24,432 --> 00:20:26,476
Oh, never mind, Jesus.
Nancy Kerrigan sucks.

503
00:20:27,894 --> 00:20:29,812
You know, somebody once said,

504
00:20:29,938 --> 00:20:33,149
"Don't try to be a great man.
Just be a man."

505
00:20:33,274 --> 00:20:35,944
Who said that?
- You did, Jesus.

506
00:20:39,072 --> 00:20:40,740
You're right, Stan.

507
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:42,200
Thank you, boys.

508
00:20:44,786 --> 00:20:46,204
Wow, did he say that
in the Bible?

509
00:20:46,329 --> 00:20:48,289
No, I saw it on "Star Trek."
- Hmm.

510
00:20:49,749 --> 00:20:52,877
C'mon, sissy, hit me!
Hit me.

511
00:20:53,002 --> 00:20:55,713
Okay, pal, you asked for it.

512
00:21:01,761 --> 00:21:04,472
Oh, you got me.

513
00:21:04,597 --> 00:21:06,891
One, two, three...

514
00:21:07,016 --> 00:21:09,394
No way!
He barely touched him.

515
00:21:09,519 --> 00:21:11,271
Seven, eight...
- Aww, come on!

516
00:21:11,396 --> 00:21:12,689
Nine, ten.
- This is ridiculous.

517
00:21:12,814 --> 00:21:13,815
You're out!

518
00:21:15,817 --> 00:21:18,236
Our savior!
- The winner by knockout

519
00:21:18,361 --> 00:21:22,699
and still undisputed ruler
of your spiritual kingdom.

520
00:21:22,824 --> 00:21:24,450
Jesús

521
00:21:24,575 --> 00:21:27,120
"El Savior"

522
00:21:27,245 --> 00:21:28,830
Christ.

523
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:32,792
Hey, he isn't hurt.
He took a dive.

524
00:21:32,917 --> 00:21:34,752
He threw the fight.
- Yeah!

525
00:21:34,877 --> 00:21:37,213
Fools.
You are all fools.

526
00:21:37,338 --> 00:21:39,048
Of course I took a dive.

527
00:21:39,173 --> 00:21:40,925
Don't you see?
Who do you think was

528
00:21:41,050 --> 00:21:44,595
the one person
that bet on Jesus to win?

529
00:21:46,389 --> 00:21:48,099
Me, you idiots.

530
00:21:48,224 --> 00:21:50,643
And now I will take all
your hard-earned money,

531
00:21:50,768 --> 00:21:53,479
and return to hell a much
richer Prince of Darkness

532
00:21:53,604 --> 00:21:56,357
and buy some real estate.
Ha, ha,ha, ha!

533
00:21:56,482 --> 00:21:57,859
I don't believe this!

534
00:21:57,984 --> 00:22:00,028
Yeah.
What a mean thing to do.

535
00:22:00,153 --> 00:22:01,904
Farewell, fools.

536
00:22:02,030 --> 00:22:05,575
Man, that guy is a jerk.

537
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:07,618
Jesus told you guys
not to bet on Satan.

538
00:22:07,744 --> 00:22:09,662
Boy, did we get screwed.

539
00:22:09,787 --> 00:22:11,622
Jesus, we're sorry.

540
00:22:11,748 --> 00:22:14,709
Can you ever forgive us?

541
00:22:14,834 --> 00:22:17,295
Aw, heck,
do I have a choice?

542
00:22:19,339 --> 00:22:21,799
Well Jesus,
I definitely learned my lesson.

543
00:22:21,924 --> 00:22:24,385
Never bet on evil
because when you do--

544
00:22:24,510 --> 00:22:25,928
Ned, look!

545
00:22:26,054 --> 00:22:28,014
There's a rare
duck-billed platypus!

546
00:22:28,139 --> 00:22:29,766
It's coming right for us!

547
00:22:32,143 --> 00:22:34,062
Oh, my God.
They killed Kenny.

548
00:22:34,187 --> 00:22:35,563
You bastard!

549
00:22:35,688 --> 00:22:37,231
Well, good-bye, guys.

550
00:22:37,357 --> 00:22:38,733
It was nice
getting to know you.

551
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:40,818
You're leaving already?
- I have to.

552
00:22:40,943 --> 00:22:43,488
My dad is always on the move.
- Wow.

553
00:22:43,613 --> 00:22:45,114
I feel kind of bad
for that kid.

554
00:22:45,239 --> 00:22:46,574
Yeah, just when
he was being accepted

555
00:22:46,699 --> 00:22:48,242
he has to leave
and start over.

556
00:22:48,368 --> 00:22:50,203
Parents can be so cruel.
Don't they realize that

557
00:22:50,328 --> 00:22:52,872
what a child needs more
than anything is security?

558
00:22:53,623 --> 00:22:55,083
More pie, hon?

559
00:22:57,251 --> 00:23:00,963
No...more...pie.

